A||||3||Ironhorse||Wire harness||||4||
Z||000000||Ironhorse||04-22-2000||11:59 PM||||hey Y'all... I'm in process of removing the engine from the fiero.... I would like to know how to disconnect the wireharness that's in the fire wall... I'm afraid to break thema nd would like to know the right way to disconnect them... The hayes book didn't explain SH*T!!!... Thanks  BTW, keep up the good work with this forums  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||4
Z||000001||fieroshop||04-23-2000||02:51 AM||||Whenever we take out an engine we take everything including the wiring harness. Disconnect the wiring harness at the ECM and also by the battery you will find a junction block. In the middle of the junction block there is a 1/4 inch bolt. With a 1/4 inch socket undo it and you then take the two halfe apart and then you disconnect the wires under the block. Also you must feed the disconnected wiring harness from the ECM and just drape all the wires over the engine.||||reg||1
Z||000002||Ironhorse||04-23-2000||11:04 AM||||Fieroshop or anyone else... Is that all, just disconnect the ecm and snake it thru the firewall.... what about the other wire harness that feed through the center console?  Just leave that alone or would I have to take out the whole thing and snake it thru the firewall hole too?||||reg||1
Z||000003||fieroshop||04-23-2000||11:48 AM||||Leave the other alone, you will also see that behind the air cleaner there is some relays and a sensor on the air breather can. Unplug the sensor and what I always do is take out the relays along with the wiring in that section. They are held by 2 small 7mm bolts.<BR>If you any other questions please feel free to call me and I can describe better. My number is on my website.  <A HREF="http://www.fieroshop.net" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fieroshop.net</A> <p>[This message has been edited by fieroshop (edited 04-23-2000).]||||reg||1
